<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Paz, Baja California Sur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-paz">La Paz</a> is a port city on the Gulf of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and the capital of the Mexican state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baja-california">Baja California</a> Sur. Spanish attempts to settle its bay began with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a> in 1535. In November 1853 the American filibuster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a> landed there and proclaimed the Republic of Lower California, before moving north and abandoning the venture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-paz-baja-california-sur.jpg" alt="La Paz, Baja California Sur" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ProtoplasmaKid · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_a%C3%A9rea_del_Museo_de_Arte_de_Baja_California_Sur_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
